  "articleBody": "It's frustrating when you put effort into your content, only to find it's not showing up in Google AI Overviews or other AI features. Many businesses wonder if they're missing some secret AI trick or special markup. The truth is, Google itself says there are no extra eligibility requirements or unique schema just for these AI features. It really comes down to solid SEO fundamentals. AI systems are looking for clear, factual, well-structured content that directly answers people's questions. If your content isn't hitting those marks, or if it's buried in a slow, complex website, it's tough for AI to find and cite it. Think about it: if a human struggles to find the answer on your page, an AI probably will too. \n\nA common mistake businesses make is creating content for every keyword variation under the sun, rather than focusing on genuine questions and providing clear, concise answers. This often leads to thin, low-value pages that AI systems are unlikely to prioritize. Another issue is relying on heavy CMS themes that slow down crawlers, or not systematically targeting the actual questions people ask on platforms like Reddit or Quora. AI Visibility Solutions focuses on deeply researching these real questions and building content specifically designed to be easily consumed and cited by AI. \n\nWhat to Do Next:\nFirst, make sure your content genuinely answers specific questions. Go through your existing pages and ask yourself: 'Does this directly answer a common customer query?' Next, check your website's technical health. Is it fast? Is it easy for crawlers to access? If you have many locations, a complex site, or have faced search penalties in the past, professional help becomes important. They can help you identify content gaps, improve site structure, and ensure your content is presented in a way that AI systems can readily understand and cite, turning your expertise into machine-readable answers.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
